# Atellar conventions

## Code style

- Minimal, modern, solid code. Do **not** over-split files or abstractions.
- Match existing naming and patterns. Read files before editing.
- Docs and code comments: **English**. User-facing chat: **Turkish**.
- Do not auto-commit unless explicitly asked.

## Repository layout

```
cmd/api          control plane
cmd/agent        node agent (atellar-agent)
cmd/atelctl      operator CLI
internal/modules nodes, containers (domain)
internal/agent   everything on-node (config, grpcclient, overlay, runtime)
internal/atelctl atelctl command logic
internal/cluster/ipam  control-plane overlay IPAM only
internal/grpc    server, agentregistry, gen
pkg/client       global HTTP API client (extend stub; no internal/client/controlplane)
```

**Dependency direction: top → down.** `agent/*` must NOT import `modules/*` or domain entities. Agent overlay uses local DTOs.

**Never** put node network code under `pkg/` or a generic `internal/pkg/`. Future: `internal/agent/netns`, `internal/agent/vmnet`.

## Transport split

| Component | Transport |
|-----------|-----------|
| `atellar-agent` | gRPC only to control plane |
| `atelctl`, plugins | HTTP via `pkg/client.AtellarClient` |
| Control plane | HTTP `:8080` + gRPC `:9090` |

## pkg/client

- Build on `pkg/client/client.go` stub (`AtellarClient`, `Token`, `Secret`, `EnsureToken()`).
- Single global HTTP client for all external API calls. Own JSON DTOs in `pkg/client/types.go` — do not import `internal/modules`.
- No separate `internal/client/controlplane` package.

## atelctl CLI

Binary name: **atelctl** (`cmd/atelctl`). Structure: `atelctl <domain> <action>`.

```
atelctl agent install|join|renew-key
atelctl cluster nodes list|containers list
```

### agent install

- Creates `/etc/atellar`, `/var/log/atellar`, systemd unit `atellar-agent.service`, enables service.
- Expects binary already at **`/usr/local/bin/atellar-agent`** — no `--agent-bin`, no `--target`, no `--config` flags.
- `--auto-join`: after install, chain directly into `Join()` (same code path as `agent join`).
- With `--auto-join`, required flags: `--join-token`, `--name`, `--public-ip`, `--private-ip`, `--control-plane-address`, `--http-port`, `--grpc-port`.

### agent join

- Registers node via HTTP (`http://address:http_port`), writes **`/etc/atellar/agent.json`**, restarts agent.
- Required: `--join-token`, `--name`, `--public-ip`, `--private-ip`, `--control-plane-address`, `--http-port`, `--grpc-port`.
- Config fields: `control_plane_address`, `http_port`, `grpc_port` (all required). Agent gRPC dials `address:grpc_port`.
- Use **`--join-token`** (not `--token`). Use `pkg/client.ControlPlane` for URL/addr helpers.

### cluster commands

- Required: `--control-plane-address`, `--http-port`, `--grpc-port`.

### Fixed paths (no CLI overrides)

| Path | Value |
|------|-------|
| Agent binary | `/usr/local/bin/atellar-agent` |
| Agent config | `/etc/atellar/agent.json` |
| Agent logs | `/var/log/atellar` |

### Naming (CLI vars)

Use descriptive names: `heartbeatInterval`, `controlPlaneAddress`, `httpPort`, `grpcPort`, `nodeName`, `publicIP`, `privateIP`, `containerdSocket`, `joinToken`.

Validation: `client.ControlPlane.Validate()` + `agent.ValidateJoinOptions()`.

## Agent

- Reads only `/etc/atellar/agent.json`. No env vars.
- Dumb node worker: config + gRPC stream + overlay reconcile + containerd (no orchestration decisions).
- Config is filled by **`atelctl agent join`** (or install `--auto-join`), not by install alone.

## Docs

Keep `docs/cli.md`, `docs/code-layout.md`, `docs/agent.md` aligned with these rules when changing CLI or layout.
